        "original_id": "d1b2150d-8936-5386-8cd0-0d3cc9a93825",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francis Knyvett Leighton\n- Organizations: All Souls College, Oxford; University of Oxford\n- Places: Oxford; England\n- Roles: English academic; priest; Warden of All Souls College, Oxford\n\nFacts:\n- Francis Knyvett Leighton was born in 1806.\n- All Souls College, Oxford, is officially named The Warden and the College of the Souls of All Faithful People Deceased in the University of Oxford.\n- All Souls College, Oxford, is a constituent college of the University of Oxford in England.\n- Francis Knyvett Leighton was an English academic and priest.\n- Francis Knyvett Leighton became Warden of All Souls College, Oxford, in 1858.\n- Francis Knyvett Leighton died on 13 October 1881.\n- Francis Knyvett Leighton served as Warden of All Souls College, Oxford, from 1858 until his death in 1881.",
